# Linkary Invited-Beta Stabilization Mode

## Scope
- Treat product as feature-frozen.
- Handle only one blocker at a time.
- Prioritize production-safe, minimal, reversible fixes.

## Allowed Work
- Blocker bugs and broken routes
- Auth/session/cookie/env/deployment issues
- CRM sync workflow failures
- Misleading empty/error states that block users
- Launch-critical copy clarifications only

## Explicitly Out Of Scope
- New features
- Redesign/polish passes
- Onboarding changes
- Referral/distribution changes
- Analytics model changes
- Org authority model changes
- Active context architecture changes

## Required Blocker Response Format
1. Root cause
2. Exact files touched
3. Any migration needed
4. Any env/config issue
5. Regression risk
6. Final verification of the fixed blocker

## Triage Inputs (collect first)
- blocker route/flow
- user type
- expected behavior
- current behavior
- exact error text
- screenshot context
- environment
- recent deploy/migration/env state

## Operating Principles
- No unrelated churn.
- Keep changes focused to the reported blocker.
- Prefer server-side observability for production triage.

## Launch-Critical UI Clarity
- In user-facing CRM tables and cards, show participant identity as handle/display name (e.g. `@username`) instead of raw profile UUIDs.
- Raw IDs are allowed only as explicit fallback when profile identity fields are unavailable.
